    </category>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q01</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q01&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which sequence has a constant multiplicative ratio?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>3, 6, 12, 24</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Each term is multiplied by 2, so it is exponential.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>3, 6, 9, 12</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This has a constant difference of 3.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>20, 17, 14, 11</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This has a constant difference of -3.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>1, 4, 7, 10</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This has a constant difference of 3.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q02</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q02&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In f(x) = 12(0.5)ˣ, what is the base?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>12</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is the initial value, not the base.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>0.5</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. The base is the repeated multiplication factor inside the exponent.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>6</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is f(1), not the base.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>x</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The exponent is the input variable, not the base.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q03</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q03&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A table has f(0)=7, f(1)=21, f(2)=63. Which model fits?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Representation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table border=1 cellpadding=4 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;x&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;0&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;1&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;2&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;f(x)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;7&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;21&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;63&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 3(7)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This reverses the initial value and base.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 7 + 14x</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The differences do not remain constant, so a linear model does not fit.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 7(3)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. The initial value is 7 and each output is multiplied by 3.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 21(3)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This uses f(1) as the initial value.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q04</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q04&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For f(x) = 4(5)ˣ, what is f(2)?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>40</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This uses 5 times 2 instead of 5 squared.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>25</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This ignores the initial value 4.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>500</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This multiplies by an extra factor of 5.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>100</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Compute 4 times 25 to get 100.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q05</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q05&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What does the 9 represent in A(t) = 9(2)ᵗ?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>Initial amount</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. At t = 0, A(0) = 9, so it is the starting value.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>Growth factor</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The growth factor is 2.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>Time interval</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The variable t represents time.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>Final amount</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The final amount depends on the value of t.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q06</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q06&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A quantity starts at 10 and is multiplied by 4 each step. Which function models it?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>g(x) = 4(10)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This reverses the starting value and multiplier.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>g(x) = 10(4)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. The starting value is 10 and the repeated multiplier is 4.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>g(x) = 10 + 4x</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This uses repeated addition instead of multiplication.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>g(x) = 40x</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is linear.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q07</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q07&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which point is always on f(x) = a(b)ˣ?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>(0, b)</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The base is not the output at x = 0 unless a = b.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>(1, a)</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>At x = 1, the output is ab.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>(0, a)</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Since b⁰ = 1, f(0) = a.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>(b, a)</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This confuses the base with an input value.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q08</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q08&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If h(x) = 3(2)ˣ, what is h(4)?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>24</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This uses 2 cubed instead of 2 to the fourth power.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>16</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This ignores the factor 3.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>81</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This incorrectly raises 3 to the fourth power.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>48</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Compute 3 times 16 to get 48.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q09</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q09&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A graph crosses the y-axis at 15 and multiplies by 1.2 each step. Which model fits?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 15(1.2)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. The y-intercept is the initial value and 1.2 is the repeated factor.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 1.2(15)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This reverses the initial value and base.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 15 + 1.2x</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is linear.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 16.2ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This combines the parameters incorrectly.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q10</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q10&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which statement describes f(x) = 2(3)ˣ?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>The output increases by 3 each step.</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>That would describe a linear pattern.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>The output triples when x increases by 1.</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. The base 3 means each step multiplies the output by 3.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>The initial value is 3.</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The initial value is 2.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>The output is always 6.</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The output changes as x changes.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q11</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q11&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which model has initial value 8 and base 5?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>y = 5(8)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This reverses the initial value and base.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>y = 8 + 5x</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is linear.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>y = 8(5)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. The coefficient 8 is the initial value and 5 is the base.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>y = 40ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This combines the values incorrectly.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q12</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q12&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is the common ratio of 2, 14, 98, 686?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>12</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is the first difference, not the ratio.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>14</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is the second term, not the common ratio.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>49</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is 7 squared, not the step ratio.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>7</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Each term is multiplied by 7.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q13</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q13&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which context is exponential?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>A culture triples every day.</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Tripling each day is repeated multiplication.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>A tank loses 5 gallons each hour.</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Losing a fixed amount is linear.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>A runner adds 2 miles each week.</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Adding a fixed amount is linear.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>A fee increases by 4 dollars each month.</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Adding a fixed dollar amount is linear.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q14</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q14&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If f(0)=11 and the base is 2, which function fits?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 2(11)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This reverses the parameters.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 11(2)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. The initial value is 11 and the repeated factor is 2.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 11 + 2x</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is linear.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 22x</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is proportional, not exponential.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q15</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q15&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For f(x)=5(2)ˣ, what is the ratio f(3)/f(2)?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>5</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is the initial value.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>10</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is f(1), not the ratio.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>2</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Consecutive outputs are multiplied by the base, which is 2.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>20</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is f(2), not the ratio between consecutive terms.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q16</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q16&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which expression represents three repeated doublings of 9?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>9 + 2 + 2 + 2</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This uses repeated addition.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>2(9)&amp;#179;</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This raises the initial value instead of using repeated doubling.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>9(3)&amp;#178;</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This uses the wrong repeated factor.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>9(2)&amp;#179;</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Three doublings multiply 9 by 2 three times.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q17</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q17&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;What is f(1) for f(x)=a(b)ˣ?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>ab</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Substituting x = 1 gives a times b.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>a</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>That is f(0).</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>b</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This ignores the initial factor a.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>a + b</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The model multiplies, not adds.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q18</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q18&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;A table has outputs 100, 50, 25, 12.5. What is the base?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Representation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table border=1 cellpadding=4 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Term&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;1&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;2&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;3&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;4&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Output&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;100&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;50&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;25&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;12.5&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>2</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>That is the reciprocal of the factor.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>0.5</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Each output is half the previous output.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>50</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is the second output, not the ratio.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>-50</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>The output decreases by multiplying by 0.5, not subtracting 50 every time.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q19</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q19&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which function has y-intercept 6?&lt;/p&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 3(6)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This has y-intercept 3.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 6x + 3</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is not exponential.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 6(3)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. The y-intercept is f(0), which equals the coefficient 6.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>f(x) = 18(3)ˣ</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This has y-intercept 18.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name>
      <text>ALG2_U04_L01_Q20</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Question ID:&lt;/strong&gt; ALG2_U04_L01_Q20&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MLA Standard:&lt;/strong&gt; MLA.A2.EX.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Which table fits f(x)=2(4)^x for x=0,1,2?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Representation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;table border=1 cellpadding=4 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;x&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;0&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;1&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;2&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;f(x)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;8&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;32&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;</text>
    </questiontext>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>4, 8, 12</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This is linear.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>2, 6, 10</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This adds 4 each time.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text>8, 32, 128</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>This starts at f(1), not f(0).</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text>2, 8, 32</text>
      <feedback format="html">
        <text>Correct. Evaluate 2(4)ˣ at x = 0, 1, 2.</text>
      </feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
</quiz>